the big fight between Oberyn Martell and the
Mountain. There were a lot of things I wasn't

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.610
able to fit in my video last night so as I
answer questions in this video I'll try to

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.880
work extra stuff in.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.110
And if you didn't hear the news, Gwendoline
Christie who plays Brienne, is going to be

00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:24.110
in Star Wars Episode 7. I'll talk about that
in my Star Wars video tomorrow.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:29.980
Congratulations to Razz Ransom, you're this
week's winner of the giveaway. You win a $20

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.890
amazon gift card. I'll DM you on your channel
for details. If you're finding me for the

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:35.229
first time I do weekly giveaways just as a
way to say thank you to all you guys for being

00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:35.510
awesome.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:40.040
Question Time! I'll see if I can squeeze more
than I normally do in. Careful for spoilers

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:45.729
from the episode if you haven't seen it. Question
1 - Thomas asks, what are Arya and The Hound

00:00:45.729 --> 00:00:47.640
going to do now?

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.640
I think by the end of the season they'll do
their plot like it is in the books. For book

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.729
readers, please use the spoiler below the
fold method if you want to make specific references.

00:00:57.729 --> 00:01:02.460
I was really happy when they started prolonging
their story, I think the two of them work

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:06.080
really well together. Loving characters on
Game of Thrones is dangerous though. You never

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.930
know who is going to die next. There's really
only two hours left in the season, but I fully

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:13.910
expect to see more Arya and Hound right up
until the finale.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:16.370
Question 2 - Chris Todd asks Where's the Blackfish?

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:19.660
Yeah, we haven't seen him since his wedding
night...duh duh duh.

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:24.430
He's still alive, he's just a captive of the
Freys along with Greatjon Umber. I don't know

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:26.750
if we'll see him again before the end of the
season?

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.550
Question 3 - Jennie asks Will Arya and Sansa
meet

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:36.390
It really seemed like the show wanted us to
believe it might happen, but I think Arya

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:40.210
and the Hound will turn right around and go
somewhere else. As for Sansa and Littlefinger,

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:45.070
she said "Shall we go" and she dyed her hair
like in the books. So I think they'll be taking

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:49.740
Robyn on that big tour of his lands like he
was talking about with Yohn Royce.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.729
Littlefinger really just wants to keep Robyn
under his thumb and it's harder to do that

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:58.000
when he's surrounded by palace guards. The
guards obey Robyn, not Littlefinger, so if

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:04.370
Robyn threw a tantrum and wanted to make people
fly, the guards would do it. Thus, Littlefinger

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:09.220
takes him away from the Moon Door.
Question 4 - Mamobster asks Isn't Cersei's

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:12.790
daughter still in Dorne, will this be bad
for her?

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:18.930
Prince Doran has a very cool head compared
to Oberyn and the Sand Snakes. Yes, people

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:23.790
are flipping out, just look at Ellaria's face.
This face is all of their faces. But they're

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.140
waiting till Season 5 to deal with a lot of
what actually ends up happening. So you'll

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.250
have to read book 4 and 5 if you don't want
to wait.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.050
But I don't think the Martells would ever
hurt a child, Myrcella is engaged to Prince

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:39.300
Doran's son and Oberyn even said point blank
she was safe when Cersei and Tywin were up

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.310
in his face at the Purple Wedding.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:46.670
It's not like Joffrey tormenting Sansa in
King's Landing. And just for reference, Myrcella

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.910
is younger than Sansa. If you look at her
in this picture though, it seems like the

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:55.069
show will age her up, just because the actress
who plays her is growing up so fast. That

00:02:55.069 --> 00:02:58.740
happens with young actors like Tommen.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.260
Question 5 - Jake Ashmore (no avatar) asks
what's going to happen to Tyrion now that

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:05.959
Oberyn is dead and is the Mountain Dead?

00:03:05.959 --> 00:03:11.250
Technically Tyrion lost the trial by combat,
because Oberyn died before the Mountain. So

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:15.790
he's sentenced to death. Right after that
all went down he would have been escorted

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:20.810
back to the Black Cells to wait for Ilyn Payne
to chop his head off Ned Stark style.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:25.150
The Mountain as far as we know is still alive
and is just gushing blood from all the pike

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:30.620
wounds. Part of the reason he's so hard to
kill is because he has such high body mass.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:34.840
The weird thing about Game of Thrones is,
unless you see their head leave their body

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:39.530
or, their skull gets squished like a grape.
They're not dead. And if you're in the North,

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:42.910
because of White Walker Necromancy, you're
only confirmed dead if you get burned to ashes.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:48.160
Question 6 - Ariadna asks did you think Daenerys
Over Reacted to Ser Jorah?

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:52.290
To be fair, most people probably would have
chopped his head off. She's just getting used

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:56.900
to being a queen and is really insecure. Hizdhar
and all the other slaving families are giving

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:01.790
her problems and the Wise Masters still need
to be dealt with. Plus she just came off of

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:05.910
the high she got from crucifying all those
people when she entered the city.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:12.060
So combine insecurity with bloodlust and you
get murderous rage. Remember who her father

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:17.150
was, she's not like the mad king at all, but
I think her reaction was appropriate.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:20.479
Once you catch someone lying, how can you
ever really know whether or not they're not

00:04:20.479 --> 00:04:25.020
lying. So if Ser Jorah wants back in the trust
circle, he's going to have to do something

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.319
pretty epic.

00:04:26.319 --> 00:04:31.449
Question 7 - Camille asks what happened between
Sansa and Baelish in her room after the camera

00:04:31.449 --> 00:04:33.809
left?

00:04:33.809 --> 00:04:40.300
I think he just left, I actually saw a bunch
of you wondering whether or not they had sex.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.719
I don't think they did. In the books when
this was happening that wasn't the case, George

00:04:44.719 --> 00:04:49.990
RR Martin spells it out more explicitly. I
think the show is just being more ambiguous

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.469
about it with those crazy long looks.

00:04:52.469 --> 00:04:58.389
I think they just have an understanding now,
that she's not going to trust him, but she

00:04:58.389 --> 00:05:03.740
trusts everyone else even less. So think of
them more as temporary allies. She needs all

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:07.580
the help she can get, and I think she senses
that Littlefinger isn't going to torture her

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:11.610
like the Lannisters.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:16.669
Question 8 - Sergio asks what would have happened
if Jaime hadn't have lost his hand and fought

00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:19.319
as Tyrion's Champion?

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:25.349
I don't think Tywin Lannister would have ever
permitted it to go down. He would have engineered

00:05:25.349 --> 00:05:29.819
some plot to keep Jaime from stepping into
the ring. He's more than happy to be done

00:05:29.819 --> 00:05:34.619
with Tyrion, but Jaime is still his prize.
But really if Jaime hadn't have lost his hand

00:05:34.619 --> 00:05:37.809
everything that happened to him and Brienne
would have gone down differently.

00:05:37.809 --> 00:05:43.339
I still think he would have kept Brienne safe,
but he wouldn't have been as open to turning

00:05:43.339 --> 00:05:47.930
his life around. He would still be the asshole
he was before he lost his hand.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:52.089
But there's no way he would have ever fought
the Mountain, even if he wanted to.

00:05:52.089 --> 00:05:56.339
He did kill a person like the Mountain, he
was called the Smiling Knight. I talk about

00:05:56.339 --> 00:05:59.430
it in that Top 10 Fighters video I posted
earlier. So technically I think he would have

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:01.169
had a shot against him in a fair fight.

00:06:01.169 --> 00:06:05.819
Question 9 - Misti asks why is Stannis the
only one who's helping out at The Wall

00:06:05.819 --> 00:06:10.849
Mostly because no one else takes it seriously,
or at least no one else with the power to

00:06:10.849 --> 00:06:14.899
do something about it. But it's important
to remember that Stannis is the only person

00:06:14.899 --> 00:06:19.249
that we've seen say he's going to help out.
That doesn't mean he'll be the only person

00:06:19.249 --> 00:06:22.349
who ever helps with the White Walkers.

00:06:22.349 --> 00:06:26.839
Because the show is going to last for about
8 seasons, I don't think it will get crazy

00:06:26.839 --> 00:06:31.930
with White Walker battles until the last two.
So in the near future, it's just going to

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:35.979
be Stannis. If he doesn't make it to The Wall
at the end of this season, I think he'll get

00:06:35.979 --> 00:06:39.899
there in the first episode of Season 5.

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:44.490
Question 10 - Inkheart asks was the simple
Lannister that squished the beetles in the

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.589
books?

00:06:45.589 --> 00:06:49.869
Orson Lannister was not in the books, I think
that was Dan and Dave just trying to get all

00:06:49.869 --> 00:06:53.179
existential. Like Tyrion is at the end of
his rope and he's pretty sure he's going to

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:57.679
die this time. See the crazy look on his face
while he was telling the story. He's a little

00:06:57.679 --> 00:07:01.689
bit drunk, but he's completely out of his
mind and just wondering out loud, if there's

00:07:01.689 --> 00:07:03.520
a reason for all the violence.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:08.099
I know a lot of you thought it might just
be a metaphor for George RR Martin squishing

00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:14.369
characters just because he can. To be fair,
I think it was a little of both. Both existential

00:07:14.369 --> 00:07:17.659
and a wink to Martin.

00:07:17.659 --> 00:07:22.319
Bonus Questions, here's a couple - Will the
Bolton's take Winterfell and rule in the North

00:07:22.319 --> 00:07:25.740
and if Roose dies, does that mean Ramsay will
rule?

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:30.649
Yes, they don't need Winterfell the location
to be Wardens of the North, Roose is already

00:07:30.649 --> 00:07:37.649
the ruler of the North in title. The reality
is that the North is so big, calling yourself

00:07:38.349 --> 00:07:43.129
the ruler and all the people that live there
thinking you're their ruler are completely

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:50.129
different things. Roose is more like the Warden
of a clump of dirt in the North.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:56.529
To answer your second question, yes, Ramsay
is a Bolton and his heir now. So everything

00:07:56.529 --> 00:07:58.770
of Roose's will pass to him when he dies.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:02.469
And last one, Ashley asks, was the Fight Scene
like it was in the books?

00:08:02.469 --> 00:08:07.649
Pretty much, in the books thought the Mountain
punches Oberyn so hard his face breaks apart

00:08:07.649 --> 00:08:12.649
and his eyes pop out of his skull. I don't
think he squished him. I think it was just

00:08:12.649 --> 00:08:17.080
the punch that splattered him. But he did
get splattered.

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:20.889
The rest of the fight was the same as the
books, with him dancing around trying to get

00:08:20.889 --> 00:08:23.439
the confession. The dialogue he said was lifted
directly from the page.

00:08:23.439 --> 00:08:30.439
So, I hope everyone has a chance to rewatch
the episode this week just to add a little

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:37.080
more context after the shock wears off. Thanks
so much for submitting questions. These are

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:42.030
always fun to do. My next bonus video will
probably be for my favorite Prophecies. There's

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:46.460
a ton of them, so I might just do my top 10.
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

